# /etc/profile.d/cssh.sh was a regular file, and therefore a dpkg conffile, up to
# and including 0.14.0. It is program code: shipping it under /etc froze it once
# an admin edited it, so fixes stopped reaching exactly the hosts most likely to
# need them. The script now lives at /usr/lib/cerberus/cssh.sh with a symlink at
# the old path; dpkg will not drop a conffile on its own, so retire it here.
#
# rm_conffile moves the file aside in preinst -- to .dpkg-bak when the admin
# modified it, which keeps their copy for reference while the live path becomes
# the symlink to current code -- and is a no-op once the conffile is gone.
#
# The version is 0.15.0~, the release that drops the conffile, NOT 0.14.0~.
# dpkg-maintscript-helper only acts when the version upgraded FROM sorts at or
# below this value, and 0.14.0~ sorts *before* 0.14.0, so an upgrade from the
# release that last shipped the conffile would have skipped the removal. Raise
# this if the change ships later than 0.15.0: too low silently leaves the
# conffile behind for good, while too high only costs a no-op check.
rm_conffile /etc/profile.d/cssh.sh 0.15.0~ cerberus-client
